-- title:
--   Hecke algebra of TₚJ_H acting on reduced two-cusp forms
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $M\ge 1$, $H$ a subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ and $S$ a set of natural numbers, and assume [`ModularCurve.HeckeDiamondInputsHAll M H`](def/ModularCurve_XHOperators.html#L113): for every prime $\ell$ the data `HeckeInputsHAlong` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ for $M,H,\ell$ (definedness and integrality of the $\beta$- and $\alpha$-data, principality of divisors on the base-changed top function field, finiteness along $\alpha$, the fundamental identity and the norm formula), and for every $d\in(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ an automorphism of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\cdot F(\Gamma_H(M))$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ satisfying `IsDiamondAutHBar`. Write $J=$ `JH M H` for the group of degree-zero divisor classes of that base-changed $q$-expansion function field and $T_pJ$ for [`TateModule p J`](def/EllipticCurve_TateModule.html#L15), the sequences $(x_n)$ in $J$ with $p^nx_n=0$ and $px_{n+1}=x_n$. Let $\mathbb{T}$ be a commutative $\mathbb{Z}_p$-algebra with a $\mathbb{T}$-module structure on $T_pJ$ compatible with the $\mathbb{Z}_p$-structure, and let $\mathrm{op}$ assign to each generator $g$ of [`CohCarrier.Gen M S`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L13) (a symbol $T_\ell$ for $\ell$ prime with $\ell\notin S$, $\ell\nmid M$; $U_q$ for $q$ prime dividing $M$; $\langle d\rangle$ for $d\in(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$) an element $\mathrm{op}(g)\in\mathbb{T}$ acting on $T_pJ$ as `tateGenOpH`, the endomorphism induced on the Tate module by the corresponding Hecke correspondence or diamond automorphism on $J$, and assume the $\mathbb{Z}_p$-subalgebra generated by the range of $\mathrm{op}$ is all of $\mathbb{T}$. Let $r\in\mathbb{N}$, $A$ a subring of $\mathbb{C}$ and $I$ an ideal of $A$ with $p\in I$. Then there is a ring homomorphism $\tau$ from $\mathbb{T}$ to the $A/I$-linear endomorphisms of [`CuspForm.TwoCuspForms M H 2 r A I`](def/CuspForm_TwoCuspLattice.html#L133), the quotient of the $A$-span of `twoCuspIntegralSet M H 2 r A` inside $S_2(\Gamma_H(M))$ by $I$ times itself, such that $\tau(\mathrm{op}(g))=$ [`CuspForm.twoCuspGenMod I S g`](def/CuspForm_TwoCuspLattice.html#L200), the endomorphism induced on that quotient by the Hecke operator `heckeGenH` attached to $g$ on weight-two cusp forms, for every generator $g$.
--
--   This is the compatibility between the Hecke algebra acting on the $p$-adic Tate module of the Jacobian of $X_H(M)$ and the Hecke algebra acting on weight-two cusp forms, transported to the reduction modulo $I$ of a two-cusp integral lattice. It is used in the comparison of the multiplicative part of $T_pJ_H$ with two-cusp eigenspaces and with the dual of such forms, in the ordinary setting.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_ringHom_moduleEnd_twoCuspForms_apply_eq_twoCuspGenMod.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_XHOperators
import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_TwoCuspLattice

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
